.TH SAPStartSrv_upgrade_from_Filesystem_disk 7 "01 Oct 2026" "" "SAPStartSrv"
.\"
.SH NAME
.\"
SAPStartSrv_upgrade_from_Filesystem_disk \- upgrade from Filesystem on shared disk to SAPStartSrv
.PP
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\"
\fB*\fP What is the upgrade about?
.PP
It is about upgrading an HA cluster for SAP central service instances from the
Filesystem resource based setup with shared disk to the simple-mount setup.
.PP
The upgrade is done in two phases:
.PP
.RS 2
1. Change the Filsystem based setup from shared disks to NFS shares,
.br
   described in this manual page.
.PP
2. Upgrade from filesystem based setup to simple-mount setup,
.br
   described in SAPStartSrv_upgrade_from_Filesystem(7).
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fP What will be changed?
.PP
This will be changed during the first phase:
.PP
.RS 2
a. SAP instance directories will be moved from shared disk to NFS shares
.br
b. Filesystem resources will changed from shared disk to NFS shares
.RE
.PP
This will be changed during the second phase:
.PP
.RS 2
a. Two systemd services sapping and sappong will be enabled.
.br
b. The SAP instance working directories for enqueue service (ASCS or SCS) and
enqueue replicator (ERS) will be added to fstab on both cluster nodes, and mounted
statically. 
.br
c. The Filesystem resources for ASCS and ERS will be removed from CIB.
.br 
d. Instead, SAPStartSrv resources for ASCS and ERS will be added to the CIB.
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fP How does the first phase look like at a glance?
.PP
The first phase consists of TODO steps:
.PP
.RS 2
1.1 Backing up the SAP instance directories.
.br
1.2 Checking for clean state, collecting information.
.br
1.3 Preparing shares on central NFS server.
.PP
2.1 Setting cluster into maintenance, saving old CIB.
.br
2.2 Stopping ERS instance, not resource group.
.br
2.3 Copying ERS instance directory to NFS share on other node.
.br
2.4 Unmounting disk-based ASCS instance directory.
.br
2.5 Adapting Filesystem resource for ERS.
.br
2.6 Starting ERS instance on other node.
.PP
\fBThe next step will bring down SAP central services.\fR
.PP
3.2 Stopping ASCS instance, not resource group.
.br
3.3 Copying ASCS instance directory to NFS share on other node.
.br
3.4 Unmounting disk-based ASCS instance directory.
.br
3.5 Adapting Filesystem resource for ASCS.
.br
3.6 Starting ASCS instance on other node.
.br
3.7 Getting cluster out of maintenance, saving new CIB.
.PP
4.1 Checking for clean state.
.br
4.2 Testing ERS instance (optional).
.RE
.PP
TODO downtime
.PP
\fB*\fP How does the second phase look like at a glance?
.PP
Please refer to manual page SAPStartSrv_upgrade_from_Filesystem(7).
.PP
\fB*\fP What needs to be prepared upfront?
.PP
First, make yourself familiar with concepts, components and configuration of the
simple-mount HA scenario for SAP central services. Refresh your knowledge of the
Filesystem resource based HA scenario.
.PP
Next, the following information needs to be collected and documented before upgrading
a cluster:
.PP
.RS 2
1. Names of cluster nodes
.br
2. Names of SAP instance directories
.br
3. Names of shared disks, LVs, VGs for the SAP instance directories
.br
4. Names of NFS server and shares for the SAP instance directories, mount options
.br
5. Names of Filesystem resources and resource groups
.br
6. Deviation of configuration from setup guide, if existing
.br
7. Matching with REQUIREMENTS section below 
.RE
.PP
Finally, prepare config templates with correct values for the given cluster.
Ideally also all needed commands are prepared in detail.
.\" TODO SAPStartSrv-upgrade-from-Filesystem-demo.8 ?
.PP
.\"
.SH EXAMPLES
.\"
.PP
\"
.SH FILES
.\"
.TP
/etc/fstab
filesystem table, for statically mounted NFS shares
.TP
/usr/sap/$SID/$Instance/
SAP instance directories, f.e. /usr/sap/EN2/ASCS00/
.TP
/usr/sap/$SID/SYS/
SAP system central local directory
.TP
/sapmnt/$SID/
SAP system central shared NFS directory
.PP
